SUMMARY:Mariachi Bonitas is Live at The HIVE
DESCRIPTION:Sacramento-based all-female mariachi\, Mariachi Bonitas\, takes the stage during The HIVE Tasting Room & Kitchen’s outdoor concert\, Live at The HIVE\, on Friday\, October 30\, from 5:30 to 8:30 p.m. Located at 1221 Harter Ave. in Woodland\, Calif.\, The HIVE is Northern California’s largest honey and mead tasting room. \nChanging the narrative of mariachi in Sacramento and beyond\, Mariachi Bonitas de Dinorah Klingler is redefining what it means to be mariachi. This all-female ensemble is challenging stereotypes in a genre long dominated by men. With a deep commitment to musical excellence and a passion for elevating the voices of women in mariachi music\, Mariachi Bonitas honors tradition while embracing innovation. \n  \n“Live at The HIVE started as a way to celebrate the positive power of bringing people together. It’s a chance for people of all ages and backgrounds to gather together and enjoy great music and food in our beautiful pollinator gardens\,” explains Shoshana Zeldner\, Director of Brand Strategy at Z Specialty Food. \n  \nIn addition to phenomenal music\, guests can explore The HIVE’s expansive pollinator gardens\, savor a seasonal farm-to-fork menu\, sip craft honey-brewed beverages and enjoy complimentary honey tastings. Family- and dog-friendly\, Live at The HIVE welcomes guests of all ages. A sliding-scale cover charge of $0-$20 per person helps keep the experience accessible and welcoming to everyone in the community. \nFounded in 2020 by the accomplished singer\, songwriter\, and musician Dinorah Klingler\, Mariachi Bonitas is built on more than twenty years of leading the way in all female mariachi.  Klinger started her musical journey with her guitar in Mexico City when she was nine years old. For fun\, Klinger and her sisters would go to subways and buses to put on performances. After taking professional music lessons\, she moved to Los Angeles as a 20 year old and joined an all-female mariachi called Mariachi Las Adelitas. Soon after\, Klinger formed her own all-female mariachi\, Mariachi Las Alondras who performed with stars such as Stevie Wonder\, Sheila E\, Patty LaBelle\, and Celia Cruz. Twenty years later\, Klinger moved to northern California and formed a new all-female mariachi\, Mariachi Bonitas de Dinorah Klingler in Sacramento\, California. \n  \nLive at The HIVE culminates during The HIVE’s 5th Anniversary Party featuring music by Wolf Jett on Saturday\, November 14. For more information visit thehivewoodland.com. \nThe HIVE Tasting Room & Kitchen is open Wednesday\, Thursday\, Sunday 11 a.m. – 3 p.m. and Friday – Saturday 11 a.m. – 7 p.m.. \nZ Specialty Food is home to Island of the Moon Honey and Moon Shine Trading Co.\, all based at The HIVE Tasting Room & Kitchen. Founded in 1979\, Z Specialty Food offers more than 30 varietal honeys from across the US and Mexico\, honey fruit spreads\, nut butters and beehive products. Through nearly 50 years of dedication to this mission\, educational partnerships\, and events\, Z Specialty Food has become a regional and national authority on honey education\, flavor and the precious pollinators and environment needed to create every delicious jar. Visit www.zspecialtyfood.com\, and The HIVE Tasting Room & Kitchen (1221 Harter Ave in Woodland\, CA) to experience all that Z Specialty Food has to offer.
URL:https://visityolo.com/event/mariachi-bonitas-is-live-at-the-hive/
LOCATION:The HIVE / Z Specialty Food\, The HIVE Tasting Room and Kitchen
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visityolo.com/wp-content/uploads/Homepage-Blurb-the-hive-1200.jpg
END:VEVENT
